1502	// Temporarily replaces every own OBJECT-valued data "message"/"name" slot on
1503	// every Error the structured clone would otherwise serialize, and returns a
1504	// restore function that puts every original descriptor back verbatim. The
1505	// clone's Error serializer runs ABSTRACT ToString on those two slots; an
1506	// object carrying an own non-callable "toString" (an ordinary form-written
1507	// string field, no different from "label") makes that coercion throw and take
1508	// the whole clone down with it. Mask values are "" for message (the serializer
1509	// installs it as the clone's own string slot, which restoreErrorMessage then
1510	// replaces) and undefined for name (the serializer omits it, so the ordinary
1511	// dropped-key walk reattaches it). Only writable, configurable own data
1512	// properties holding an object are masked — the exact shape a successful form
